1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,983
Cinco de Mayo. Mexican Independence Day.

2
00:00:04,133 --> 00:00:06,183
Nope. Wrong day.

3
00:00:06,333 --> 00:00:09,217
Cinco de Mayo: the mix-up.

4
00:00:09,367 --> 00:00:13,650
Mexico's Independence Day is September 16.

5
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:18,017
It marks 1810, when the fight against Spain began.

6
00:00:18,167 --> 00:00:20,350
So what's the fifth of May?

7
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:23,183
A battle. 1862.

8
00:00:23,333 --> 00:00:26,250
France invaded Mexico.

9
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:30,050
The French army was one of the best in the world.

10
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:34,417
At Puebla, Mexico's smaller army won.

11
00:00:34,567 --> 00:00:36,617
A huge upset.

12
00:00:36,767 --> 00:00:41,283
France did come back, and took Mexico City a year later.

13
00:00:41,433 --> 00:00:44,883
But the victory at Puebla became a symbol.

14
00:00:45,033 --> 00:00:48,917
In Mexico, it's mostly celebrated in Puebla.

15
00:00:49,067 --> 00:00:52,050
It's much bigger in the United States.

16
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:56,483
Mexican American activists made it a day of pride.

17
00:00:56,633 --> 00:01:00,083
Then advertisers turned it into a party.

18
00:01:00,233 --> 00:01:03,517
Independence Day: September 16.

19
00:01:03,667 --> 00:01:06,550
Cinco de Mayo: a battle win.

20
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:11,117
Anyway, happy Independence Day! On May 5th.
